  "notes": "Logo is the coloured header logo (Logo-Compressed.png); the site also serves a larger version with a catchphrase (wp-content/uploads/2024/10/NC-Logo-2021-with-catchphraseArtboard-1.png) and a white version for dark backgrounds (NC-logo-wht-compressed.png). heroImage is the home page's header background (2024/11/NC10.jpg, read from the page stylesheet, not viewed); the humpback tail photo at the start of the gallery is the alternative to compare. Gallery leads with the whale photos whose file names carry Naturaliste-Charters, then the Bremer Bay carousel, the vessel, and the home page gallery. Videos: four are on the YouTube channel the site footer links to (youtube.com/channel/UCjssNut8GG3Y78kBqlBLOWA, picked from its videos page), and two are mp4 files the site hosts itself (one on the Our Vessels page, one on the Dunsborough page); channel videos that credit another person (for example one marked Courtesy: Addison Ong) and the predation clips were left out. Left out: badges, award and accreditation logos, icons, map images (map.jpg, dbmap.jpg, augustaboatharbour.jpg), the pop-up banner (2026/08/A_Departing-website_DESKTOP.jpg and MOBILE.jpg, text strips), banner-named files (dunboroughbanner.jpg), the species cut-out graphics and the 260 pixel blurb images on the home and location pages, and crew portraits. Left out because the file name credits a photographer: orca.breaching-Jodielowe-scaled.jpg (the Bremer Canyon page's own social image), Paul-Cross-Nic-Duncan.jpg and the matching NaturalisteChaters_Crossy_resized photo, and the Nic-Duncan and Dan-Mantle files on the current sightings page; a person may want to confirm whether these are the operator's own. Also left out because their origin could not be confirmed: 7150864.jpg on the home page (numeric name, may be a stock id), the scenery photos on the Augusta, Dunsborough and Bremer Bay location pages, and the 12-photo gallery on the Additional Services page (older photos whose subjects, possibly including the sister company's fishing charters, could not be checked), so Private and Custom Charters has no photos. The Bremer Canyon page carries only a handful of photos, so its list is short. No bot check, captcha or 403 was met; a few responses were a temporary 520 or 525 server error and loaded on a single retry. Nothing was downloaded."
